---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Enrollment policy extensions"
  path="/dev/enrollment-policy-extensions"
  section="dev"
  description="Add rules, actions, assignment strategies, and billing strategies without storing executable classes in policy data."
>
  <p>
    Enrollment policies store stable handler keys and JSON configuration. They
    never store PHP class names, closures, formulas, or scripts. A published
    version and every compiled enrollment snapshot are immutable.
  </p>

  <h2>Extension contracts</h2>
  <p>
    Implement one of the public contracts in <code
      >app/Contracts/Enrollment</code
    >:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>EnrollmentRuleHandler</code> evaluates an <code
        >EnrollmentContext</code
      > and returns a <code>RuleResult</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>EnrollmentActionHandler</code> performs one atomic, idempotent action
      and returns an <code>ActionResult</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>EnrollmentAssignmentStrategy</code> describes or simulates subject/class
      assignment. A strategy selected for live rollout must also implement <code
        >RuntimeEnrollmentAssignmentStrategy</code
      >.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>EnrollmentBillingStrategy</code> describes or simulates fees and payment
      gates. A strategy selected for live rollout must also implement
      <code>RuntimeEnrollmentBillingStrategy</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Keys are public compatibility identifiers. Prefix third-party keys, for
    example <code>acme.scholarship_eligibility</code>, and never rename a key
    while published policy versions still reference it.
  </p>

  <h2>Registration</h2>
  <p>
    Register handlers from a service provider after resolving <code
      >EnrollmentPolicyRegistry</code
    >:
  </p>
  <pre><code>use App\Enrollment\EnrollmentPolicyRegistry;

$this-&gt;app-&gt;afterResolving(
    EnrollmentPolicyRegistry::class,
    function (EnrollmentPolicyRegistry $registry): void &#123;
        $registry-&gt;registerRule(new ScholarshipEligibilityRule());
        $registry-&gt;registerAction(new ReserveScholarshipAction());
    &#125;,
);</code></pre>
  <p>
    Registry objects may contain immutable metadata and stateless collaborators.
    Do not store a request, user, enrollment, or tenant as mutable registry
    state; KoAkademy runs under Octane.
  </p>

  <h2>Configuration schemas</h2>
  <p>
    Return a JSON-schema-like object from <code>configurationSchema()</code> or
    <code>payloadSchema()</code>. Configuration must be plain JSON data. Reject
    unknown keys where practical and give validation messages an operator can
    act on.
  </p>
  <p>
    To make an extension editable by school operators, also implement the
    optional <code>EnrollmentOperatorSchemaProvider</code> contract. Its
    <code>operatorSchema()</code> manifest supplies help content and fields for the
    guided editor. Supported controls are boolean, text, number, money, percentage,
    date/date range, select, multi-select, role, permission, school, program, period,
    and notification channel. Dynamic choices must use one of the registry's whitelisted
    option-source keys.
  </p>
  <p>
    Extensions without this optional contract still execute and can be restored
    from a validated backup, but their configuration is shown read-only in the
    visual editor. This keeps existing community extensions compatible.
  </p>
  <p>
    The operator-schema contract is independent from runtime execution. Legacy
    assignment and billing extensions remain valid manifest and simulation
    providers, but compilation rejects them for a published live workflow unless
    they implement the corresponding runtime contract.
  </p>
  <pre><code>public function operatorSchema(): array
&#123;
    return [
        'description' =&gt; 'Allow only students with an approved scholarship.',
        'what_it_does' =&gt; 'Checks the approved scholarship percentage on the student record.',
        'impact' =&gt; 'Students below this percentage cannot continue through the matching blueprint.',
        'example' =&gt; 'Enter 50 to allow half and full scholars.',
        'docs_anchor' =&gt; 'enrollment-policies/availability-eligibility-documents',
        'fields' =&gt; [[
            'key' =&gt; 'minimum_percentage',
            'label' =&gt; 'Minimum scholarship',
            'control' =&gt; 'percentage',
            'required' =&gt; true,
            'description' =&gt; 'The smallest approved scholarship percentage accepted by this rule.',
            'placeholder' =&gt; '50',
            'example' =&gt; 50,
            'prefix' =&gt; null,
            'suffix' =&gt; '%',
            'min' =&gt; 0,
            'max' =&gt; 100,
            'step' =&gt; 1,
            'recommended' =&gt; 50,
        ]],
    ];
&#125;</code></pre>
  <p>The top-level help keys are additive and optional:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Key</th>
        <th>Operator use</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>description</code></td>
        <td>Short explanation shown on the setting card.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>what_it_does</code></td>
        <td>Plain-language explanation in the contextual help drawer.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>impact</code></td>
        <td>What changes for a matched student.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>example</code></td>
        <td>A realistic school scenario or sample value.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>docs_anchor</code></td>
        <td>Relative page under the configured documentation base URL.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Field metadata is also optional. Use <code>description</code>,
    <code>placeholder</code>, <code>example</code>, <code>prefix</code>,
    <code>suffix</code>, <code>min</code>, <code>max</code>, <code>step</code>,
    and <code>recommended</code> to make the form self-explanatory. Conditional fields
    may use a deterministic <code>visible_when</code> descriptor:
  </p>
  <pre><code>[
    'key' =&gt; 'minimum_amount',
    'label' =&gt; 'Minimum amount',
    'control' =&gt; 'money',
    'min' =&gt; 0,
    'visible_when' =&gt; [
        'field' =&gt; 'gate_type',
        'equals' =&gt; 'fixed',
    ],
]</code></pre>
  <p>
    Supported conditional operators are <code>equals</code> and <code>in</code>.
    Conditions may reference only another field in the same handler
    configuration. Do not use executable callbacks in a manifest.
  </p>

  <h2>Operator-schema compatibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Adding help text, bounds, examples, or conditional visibility is
      backward-compatible when it does not reinterpret stored values.
    </li>
    <li>
      Removing a field requires the runtime handler to keep accepting
      configurations written by every supported published schema version.
    </li>
    <li>
      Renaming a field or changing its semantics is incompatible. Add a new
      handler key or schema version instead.
    </li>
    <li>
      Missing optional metadata receives generic guidance from the registry.
    </li>
    <li>
      A handler with no operator schema remains executable and importable but
      read-only in the guided editor.
    </li>
    <li>
      Option sources are allowlisted by the application. Unknown source names
      are rejected during draft save, import, simulation, and publication.
    </li>
    <li>
      The manifest must never contain a class name to execute, a script, a
      closure, an arbitrary URL, or a request-specific object.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Rules should fail closed when required facts are unavailable. Actions run
    inside the enrollment transition database transaction and must use the
    supplied idempotency key for every externally visible side effect. They must
    not open nested transactions, change workflow status/outcome, use ambient
    <code>Auth</code>, or call the legacy workflow adapter. Queue notifications
    only after commit.
  </p>

  <h2>Import format</h2>
  <p>Exports use this envelope:</p>
  <pre><code>&#123;
    "format": "koakademy.enrollment-policy",
    "schema_version": 1,
    "name": "College enrollment",
    "configuration": &#123;&#125;
&#125;</code></pre>
  <p>
    Only <code>configuration</code> is executable by the policy compiler, and only
    through registered keys. Imports containing unknown handler keys, unsupported
    schema versions, PHP class names, or script/code fields are rejected.
  </p>

  <h2>Version compatibility</h2>
  <p>
    Handler changes must remain compatible with every published schema version
    they claim to support. Add a new stable handler key for incompatible
    semantics. Never reinterpret an existing key in a way that changes pinned
    snapshots.
  </p>

  <h2>Testing expectations</h2>
  <p>
    Every extension should include Pest coverage for metadata, valid and invalid
    configuration, pass/fail evaluation, authorization, idempotent retry,
    transaction rollback, and compatibility with an immutable compiled snapshot.
    Capacity-changing actions also need a concurrent final-seat test.
  </p>
  <p>Operator-facing extensions must additionally test:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Every supported control converts to and from stored configuration.</li>
    <li>Recommended values and numeric bounds validate correctly.</li>
    <li>
      <code>visible_when</code> hides only the intended field and server-side validation
      follows the same condition.
    </li>
    <li>Unknown option sources fail with an actionable validation message.</li>
    <li>Missing help metadata receives registry defaults.</li>
    <li>
      An extension without <code>EnrollmentOperatorSchemaProvider</code> renders read-only
      without losing stored configuration.
    </li>
    <li>Import/export contains stable keys and plain configuration only.</li>
    <li>
      A representative simulation and the published version produce the same
      resolved checksum.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    When a handler can block a student, test that its failure includes an
    operator-friendly message and the correct editor section so the simulation
    report can link back to the setting.
  </p>
  <p>
    Run focused tests first, then Pint, Wayfinder generation, the frontend
    build, and <code>git diff --check</code>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
